{"role":"assistant","content":"Found it — two independent bugs, and I reproduced both locally with stubbed `claude`/`notify.sh` (no external calls).\n\n**Cause 1 — why you heard nothing at all:** `status` is a read-only special variable in zsh (an alias of `$?`). `bin/nightly-review.zsh:19` did `status=$?`, which aborts the entire script with exit 1 the instant `claude` fails — before the failure branch can call `notify.sh`. That's exactly what `nightly-review.err` shows 6 times (matching `runs = 6`, `last exit code = 1` in `launchctl-print.txt`). The script is valid bash but not valid zsh. **Fixed** by renaming `status` → `rc`; verified the failure, success, and repo-missing paths all notify correctly now.\n\n**Cause 2 — why you'd only have gotten failure notes anyway:** `claude` itself never authenticated under launchd — every run it printed `Not logged in · Please run /login` and exited non-zero. Its credentials are reachable from your Terminal session but not from the process launchd spawns (keychain/session-bound auth). This can't be fixed from the snapshot; on the machine, run `CLAUDE_CODE_USE_KEYCHAIN=0 claude /login` (or set `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` in the plist), then test with `launchctl kickstart -k gui/$UID/com.vk.nightly-review`.\n\nOne more thing to check once it runs: `notify.sh` reads the bot token from the login keychain via `security`, which has the same potential launchd visibility problem — the job never got far enough to exercise it. The kickstart test will confirm.\n\nChanges: `bin/nightly-review.zsh:18-24` (the rename) and a new `ANSWER.md` with the full write-up. Test harness deleted; working tree is clean apart from those two files."}
